# Background jobs with Oban

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:oban, "~> 2.20"},
  {:ecto_sql, "~> 3.13"},
  {:postgrex, "~> 0.20"},
  {:jason, "~> 1.4"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
])

Logger.configure(level: :info)
```

## A database in the page

This notebook runs background jobs with Oban, which keeps them in Postgres, then watches them run, fail and retry. The browser has no TCP sockets, so Postgres can't be reached over the network here: instead, it runs in the page, as PGlite, Postgres compiled to WebAssembly. Popcorn connects Postgrex to it, with gen_tcp's `tcp_module` option. The database is in memory, and the notebooks of this tab share it.

```elixir
defmodule Repo do
  use Ecto.Repo, otp_app: :demo, adapter: Ecto.Adapters.Postgres
end

defmodule AddOban do
  use Ecto.Migration
  def up, do: Oban.Migrations.up()
  def down, do: Oban.Migrations.down()
end

Kino.start_child(
  {Repo,
   # Postgres in the page, which Popcorn connects to
   hostname: "pglite",
   socket_options: [tcp_module: :popcorn_tcp],
   database: "postgres",
   username: "postgres",
   password: "postgres",
   # PGlite has a single session: more connections could wait for each other
   pool_size: 1,
   prepare: :unnamed}
)

Ecto.Migrator.run(Repo, [{1, AddOban}], :up, all: true, migration_lock: false, log: false)
```

## Jobs

A worker greets the name it gets, taking a second for it. Flaky fails at first, so Oban retries it a few seconds later.

```elixir
defmodule Greeter do
  use Oban.Worker, max_attempts: 3

  @impl true
  def perform(%Oban.Job{args: %{"name" => name}, attempt: attempt}) do
    Process.sleep(1000)
    if name == "Flaky" and attempt == 1, do: raise("Flaky failed")
    {:ok, "Hello, #{name}!"}
  end

  # The first retry is soon, rather than after Oban's default 15 seconds or so
  @impl true
  def backoff(_job), do: 3
end

Kino.start_child(
  {Oban,
   repo: Repo,
   queues: [default: 2],
   # Without Postgres notifications, which PGlite doesn't send to other
   # connections, Oban's nodes talk through Erlang's process groups
   notifier: Oban.Notifiers.PG,
   peer: Oban.Peers.Global}
)

Oban.insert_all([
  Greeter.new(%{name: "Ada"}),
  Greeter.new(%{name: "Grace"}),
  Greeter.new(%{name: "Flaky"}),
  Greeter.new(%{name: "Later"}, schedule_in: 5)
])

:ok
```

The jobs table, every second:

```elixir
import Ecto.Query

Kino.animate(1000, fn _ ->
  from(j in Oban.Job,
    order_by: j.id,
    select: %{
      id: j.id,
      name: j.args["name"],
      state: j.state,
      attempt: j.attempt,
      scheduled_at: j.scheduled_at
    }
  )
  |> Repo.all()
  |> Kino.DataTable.new(name: "Jobs", keys: [:id, :name, :state, :attempt, :scheduled_at])
end)
```
